target: skills/review/review-loop/runlog.py
verify: cd skills/review/review-loop && ./runlog.test.sh
why:    any row appended after finish overwrites run["phase"] and resurrects a closed run, so the Stop hook blocks the next turn
--- old
        if run.get("repo") != repo or run.get("finished_at") or run.get("outcome"):
--- new
        if run.get("repo") != repo or run.get("phase") == "finish":
